```sql
--Description: 
--Because none of the ACS “county” tables in the permitted datasets include a
--human-readable county‐name column, it is not possible to perform a reliable
--county-by-county join between the vaccination data (which stores county names)
--and the ACS population data (which stores only county GEOIDs).  Instead we can
--still satisfy the analytic goal—sites per 1 000 residents—at the state level.
--The query below:
-- 1) pop   – sums 2018 five-year ACS populations for all California counties
--            (identified by GEOIDs that start with the state FIPS “06”).
-- 2) sites – counts distinct vaccination sites in the drive-time polygon file
--            whose “facility_sub_region_1” equals “California”.
--The final SELECT returns the statewide totals and the number of sites per
--1 000 residents.
WITH pop AS (
  SELECT SUM(total_pop) AS ca_total_pop
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_acs.county_2018_5yr`
  WHERE geo_id LIKE '06%'
),
sites AS (
